#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551387} :activity/id #uuid "d303828c-4774-564e-856f-3e961776778d" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049147 :topic/id #uuid "de74c316-f607-5e04-8847-2af8b65a611b" :topic/math-academy-id 3694} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551368 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77d82670-955d-5fbd-bc9e-ff9b5595ca19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463536} {:answer/id #uuid "70953006-86df-56ba-885e-a59756ac68a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463537}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463536} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bbc6ae6-a433-51b7-9bcc-4234a55196ba" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464702} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3413fb0-066c-5f24-a376-7d72fef132fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463538} {:answer/id #uuid "090b215e-b754-554a-8109-db90d4abfb27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463539}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463539} :answer-field/id #uuid "79b6f686-1017-5c39-b085-1d1f73f3ac2e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3c62597-d021-5cbd-8c81-864877afd3e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463540} {:answer/id #uuid "9d291d8d-f31c-5932-8efc-6cd6f690f503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463541}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463540} :answer-field/id #uuid "162bbeb9-8561-5809-b4fd-17fcbbfe7d72" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e9d575c8-adec-5386-bb2f-10bc638decac" :question/math-academy-id "q-125706" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a423ab56220e438fb849d2025ab53b99bb74ef598e16110c911d691680130527.png)\n\nConsider the semicircle and constant vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semicircle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I is false, while statement II is true. As the particle moves from $A$ to $B,$ the force $F$ works  against the particle for $x<0,$ while $F$  works with the particle for $x>0.$ \n\n![](images/cd/cd52e91c72d481980c9a48575da7ca3eaebd2ed27f96b1054cf5c1c5da1aa3d9.png)\n\n \nBy symmetry, the contribution to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for $x<0$ is canceled out by the contribution for $x>0.$ So, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/a1/a1e8fa5262fc787b691b3753fc57ab39aceee7c57dbbe166c6da6f6effaf42dc.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "1917119d-a3c7-5df2-a185-1f304577335a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551389}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551387 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47df525a-0d27-5474-842e-e797864d924f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459479} {:answer/id #uuid "0f4b12aa-dfc8-5cf6-bb46-fa30cda83363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459480}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459479} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ebe448c-6d78-52eb-b87a-c0f6378a526d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3a5163-4335-5da1-a308-4afc6fa83343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459481} {:answer/id #uuid "2865bf65-f4fa-5527-9338-dac5b94be08d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459482}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459482} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6785c8-4fa8-5419-98ef-b6ca891fd2fe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a7f457e-5e87-5921-9c97-354280faa2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459483} {:answer/id #uuid "58d82791-fb0b-511f-a411-3a2ed07c51ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459484}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459484} :answer-field/id #uuid "5480c90b-6e84-5672-a102-83d8323aaae1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "26c0cce0-6deb-59c6-a9c4-06e4698080d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-125381" :question/problem "![](images/50/501a3512fb4b8a1898c6dfb8816d587de4a0cd585991d9c92d2bb35d83a2853d.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semicircle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/4c/4c11b38f9e598e0cd8fc50715d2091e5bea48d188440ae8a99c84d66a6acb6b9.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/34/346007ae582fccdf4519a3d1cd50a467e19d5345238343a1311fd3348bbeb138.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "3551427b-781d-572b-8a50-737fe5febecf" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551425}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551389 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414783 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "740bd403-f1e6-5a92-a2b9-efa1ee0f552f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472742} {:answer/id #uuid "5170cfef-7833-5d81-bf15-5bd1c2583c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472743}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472742} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ab5fa05-0008-5864-bfbd-37a853fa3a21" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13931620-6744-5279-819c-a867d3d2f624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472744} {:answer/id #uuid "89f7ef7d-3d29-5bcd-86e4-6ccb6a042395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472745}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472745} :answer-field/id #uuid "0562aeab-6992-5c67-82d7-eee722fd8045" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473767} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194dcf31-6ded-5f7d-8ad4-8503fc14610b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472746} {:answer/id #uuid "cff66d04-5359-528e-90cc-f15b10b85371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472747}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472746} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cfac123-c198-5997-bc78-bc4c79e3be46" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0b65bfe0-6178-564e-825d-19d4ac9443d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-150012" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5a3961346a4bcb0d94e46caf6d6ed1253dc56fb4761db07b11829e329bc2fa8d.png)\n\nConsider the part of parabola and constant vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the part of parabola is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I is false, while statement II is true. As the particle moves from $A$ to $B,$ the force $F$ works against the particle for $x>0,$ while $F$  works with the particle for $x<0.$ \n\n![](images/af/af80eab6427f376084301c03715fd098cfe4a1c816dcd72d3e1129cfa35ff29d.png)\n\n \n\nBy symmetry, the contribution to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for $x<0$ is canceled out by the contribution for $x>0.$ So,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/a2/a26ca79400bf30aa891543d30a052a6e8ec071ccb48fcd8c418fe0a713dad212.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "398a54a2-4081-54b9-91fa-06fdfcf9e9d3"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551425 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ed18d44-37e8-529c-a585-0ceab88f3f9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550685} {:answer/id #uuid "8858c48e-583e-5419-89c1-66b239d5970c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550713} {:answer/id #uuid "b2545c5c-af10-54e4-a998-61fc386ed756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550854} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ee07b7-d7ad-5975-9eff-46b920985b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550954} {:answer/id #uuid "dc1fa96f-fbba-519c-ac7f-2711d8804739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550965}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550685} :answer-field/id #uuid "53503a6a-a2ae-508c-9eef-c15dd0d61993" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2310204a-fdf5-57d1-9e96-98189fedc070" :question/math-academy-id "q-125490" :question/problem "![](images/9f/9f94742a7f37fd7f6a1c789401a2e323fec80aca584774453cba03cf69f28ade.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/f4/f4e8c62562ee1657e41bb36a21c901dc95935558641f724f934a4c58706f4a64.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/40/40b100dd4bc71b95f5ad99eb0cec8ed87133211bb371b22deccb851f79c695b3.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "90d440b1-77fd-57a5-b7b7-bc29251c9577" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551430}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551430 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac92f55-bdd5-5ebb-8623-7211f79f9620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550395} {:answer/id #uuid "179b5f9d-873a-571a-b6bf-69376a9ef389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550418} {:answer/id #uuid "1dfb5464-e95f-5d2a-b797-775d6cf22682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550431} {:answer/id #uuid "a8026852-ad3d-5420-9b64-1828b556006e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550811} {:answer/id #uuid "d9563607-dd70-5767-87cb-3d112f17eed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550956}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550395} :answer-field/id #uuid "be155506-4e79-5a1a-866f-997f1cb30ccc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "17a8497e-763c-5804-a8ea-e63d106be3fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-125497" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4ee9e02184efd314371a99c6242540e5e2e6effc9e21d41a86648b433b8a6938.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semiellipse is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/1d/1d91a85ccbb948e070db738373ffc5032f4e91a0ba8e04cd14e79276b0e798f8.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/a8/a8e0bffd04fb7b765d3c654f62b1958ab55a42f0d26cbc9f2b2e31f7d8e6f775.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :step/id #uuid "a1c627f2-8e5c-5d6d-9e77-16402055855b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551368}}] :activity/title "Interpreting Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550361}]}
